oard file listing, so module sizes cannot be resolved reliably. This analysis was not saved.", "noSources":"No source files found in this repository.", "noPluginDir":"No published plugin directory found on gh-pages."})}), "importAnalysis":({"title":"Import Analysis", "description":"What each official extension imports from @rancher/shell and @rancher/components, read from its source at the latest released tag.", "empty":"No data. Press Refresh to run the analysis.", "notBuilt":"This analysis has not been run yet. Press Refresh to scan the official extensions. The result is saved, so later visits load it without re-scanning.", "refreshCost":"Scans every official extension repo and downloads around 1,150 source files. Takes 30–90 seconds.", "sourceNote":"Module sizes resolved against {ref}.", "selectExtension":"Extension", "unresolvedHint":"This path does not resolve to a file in rancher/dashboard, so its size is unknown.", "unresolvedDescription":"Shell paths that no longer resolve to a file in rancher/dashboard. Each is either a stale import, a path that was renamed, or something private that was never part of the public API.", "surfaceDescription":"Shell marks nothing as public or private, so every path below is API that has to keep working. These are grouped by how exposed each one is to shell changing underneath it — expand a row to see the exact symbols that would break.", "noRisky":"No extension imports a private or internal shell path. Every import is against a module path shell can reasonably be expected to keep.", "exposureTitle":"Exposure by extension", "pathsTitle":"Paths", "showAllPaths":"Show all {count} shell paths, not just the ones needing attention", "scope":({"shell":"@rancher/shell", "components":"@rancher/components"}), "symbols":({"description":"Every named export the extensions take out of @rancher/shell and @rancher/components, listed by symbol rather than by path. Filter for a name to see which extensions would have to change if it moved, changed signature or went away.", "filterLabel":"Symbol or path", "filterPlaceholder":"e.g. downloadFile, or utils/download", "showing":"Showing {shown} of {total} symbol-and-path rows — {symbols} distinct names across {extensions} extensions.", "noMatch":"No symbol or path matches that text.", "noSpecifiers":"No named imports were recorded at all. This analysis predates specifier collection, so refresh it to get symbol-level answers.", "defaultExport":"default export", "defaultHint":"The module's default export, imported under whatever local name each extension chose. Those local names are not recorded and do not matter — the default export is the thing that has to keep existing.", "cantTellLabel":"Cannot rule out", "cantTellHint":"Reach this path without naming anything — a whole-module import, a dynamic import() or a re-export — so this symbol cannot be ruled out for them: {extensions}", "noRiskHint":"The risk rules describe shell's own tree and say nothing meaningful about @rancher/components, which is published separately.", "namespaceTitle":"Paths imported whole", "namespaceDescription":"Nothing names an individual export from these, so no symbol-level answer exists for them. An extension importing a whole module could be using anything in it, and a symbol search above will never return these rows — which is exactly why they are listed here in full.", "unrecordedTitle":"Paths with no recorded names", "unrecordedDescription":"Reached only through a dynamic import() or a re-export, neither of which records which names were taken. These paths are counted but carry no symbols, which is a limit of the scanner rather than a finding about the code.", "caveatsTitle":"What this list does not tell you", "caveat":({"notUsage":"It records imports, not calls. An extension that imports a symbol and never uses it is still listed, so read the extension list as everyone who might break rather than everyone who will.", "pathCounts":"The import count is per path, not per symbol. The analysis stores one count for each path with the set of names beside it, so the number is import statements against the path the symbol came from.", "namespace":"Three import forms name nothing — a whole-module import, a dynamic import() and a re-export — so an extension using one can never be ruled out for any symbol in that module. Those extensions are counted in their own column and never folded into the used-by count.", "unrecorded":"Where a path has no named importers at all, there is no row to carry that warning, so the path is listed in its own table below instead. No symbols recorded is not the same fact as no symbols used.", "stale":"Everything here comes from the saved import analysis, read at each extension's released tag at the time it ran. An extension that has released since is described by code nobody is running."})}), "risk":({"private":"Private", "internal":"Internal", "file-suffix":"File path", "ok":"OK"}), "riskNote":({"private":"Reaches into shell's own screens or startup code, which carry no stability guarantee and can be moved or deleted in any release without anything warning the extension.", "internal":"Depends on shell's internal wiring — its store, mixins or resource models — rather than on a contract meant for consumers.", "file-suffix":"Imports a concrete file rather than a module path, so it pins the file extension. Converting that file from .js to .ts inside shell breaks this import, even though nothing about its behaviour changed.", "ok":"A plain module path with no obvious problem. It is still unversioned API, but it is the kind a supported surface would most likely keep."}), "area":({"form-components":"Form components", "formatters":"Formatters", "components":"Components", "rancher-components":"Rancher components", "utils":"Utils", "config":"Config and constants", "models":"Resource models", "store":"Store and plugins", "composables":"Composables", "mixins":"Mixins", "types":"Types and contracts", "resource-views":"Resource views", 