alysis has not been run yet. Press Refresh to read the published bundles. The result is saved, so later visits load it without re-downloading.", "refreshCost":"Downloads up to 98 MB of source maps from gh-pages. Takes several minutes.", "sourceNote":"Bundle size is total minified JS across all code-split chunks. The breakdown figures come from source maps, which record pre-minification bytes, so each is scaled to disk by its own bundle's source-to-disk ratio — that way a breakdown adds up to the bundle beside it rather than to two or three times it.", "sourceSizeHint":"Pre-minification bytes, merged across every chunk.", "notPublished":"Not published", "pluginDir":"Plugin directory", "sourceMaps":"Source maps", "selectExtension":"Extension", "noLeaks":"No extension is bundling code the host already provides.", "leaksDescription":"@rancher/shell and @rancher/components are provided by the host at runtime and must be externalized. Anything listed here is shipping a second copy of code that is already loaded.", "tabs":({"overview":"Overview", "cause":"By Cause", "duplication":"Duplication", "leaks":"Externalization", "perExtension":"Extension Detail"}), "duplication":({"description":"Packages carried by more than one published bundle. Every extension ships its own copy of whatever it was not told to externalize, so a dependency used by eight extensions is downloaded eight times over by anyone who installs all eight.", "thresholdLabel":"Minimum extensions carrying it", "threshold":"{count} extensions or more", "none":"No package is carried by that many extensions.", "hostProvided":"Host provides it", "hostProvidedHint":"The host already loads this at runtime, so every copy inside a bundle is removable rather than all but one.", "splitHint":"The carriers resolved this to different versions, so one shared copy means somebody has to move. Worth knowing before proposing it.", "noVersionHint":"No version resolved. Either the lockfile could not be read or the name is not a real package, so this is unknown rather than agreement.", "unmeasured":"Source maps could not be read for {count} analysed extension(s), so they contribute nothing to the figures below — those are summed over {measured}. Not measured: {extensions}", "unscaled":"Excluded because their source maps carried no content to measure against, so their bytes could not be scaled to disk: {extensions}", "method":"Shipped sizes are source-map bytes scaled by each bundle's own source-to-disk ratio before being summed. Across the published extensions that ratio runs from 0.30 to 0.66, so one shared figure would be wrong for almost all of them. Savings are estimates.", "savingKind":({"all-copies":"The host already provides this, so externalizing it removes every copy rather than all but one.", "all-but-one":"The host does not provide this, so externalizing it means shell shipping one shared copy. The saving is every copy but the largest."}), "summary":({"packages":"Duplicated packages", "shipped":"All copies, shipped", "saving":"Estimated saving", "shellCaused":"Of which shell-caused", "versionSplits":"With version disagreement"}), "cols":({"carriedBy":"Carried by", "allCopies":"All copies", "saving":"Saving if external"})}), "summary":({"published":"Published bundles", "totalBytes":"Total shipped JS", "largest":"Largest bundle", "leaking":"Extensions with leaks", "shellCaused":"Shell-caused weight"}), "detail":({"chunks":"Chunks", "byCause":"Why it is in the bundle", "byCategory":"By category", "byPackage":"By package", "leaked":"Should have been external"}), "warn":({"shell":"@rancher/shell is bundled — {count} file(s). The host provides it at runtime, so this is a second copy.", "components":"@rancher/components is bundled — {count} file(s). The host provides it at runtime, so this is a second copy.", "host":"Host-provided packages found in the bundle: {pkgs}"}), "category":({"shell":"@rancher/shell (should be external)", "components":"@rancher/components (should be external)", "host-provided":"Host-provided (should be external)", "extension-code":"Extension own code", "external-lib":"Bundled external library", "externalized":"Externalized", "webpack-runtime":"Webpack runtime"}), "cause":({"shell-code":"Shell code bundled", "shell-dep":"Shell dependency", "shell-dep-transitive":"Shell dependency (transitive)", "node-polyfill":"Node polyfill", "build-tooling":"Build tooling", "already-external":"Stale build (now externalized)", "extension-code":"Extension own code", "extension-dep":"Extension dependency", "generated":"Generated", "webpack-runtime":"Webpack runtime", "externalized":"Externalized"}), "causeFix":({"shell-code":"Externalize @rancher/shell in the library build.", "shell-dep":"Externalize it, or cut the shell import that drags it in. Either way the fix is in rancher/dashboard, not here.", "shell-dep-transitive":"Follows its parent; fixing the parent clears it.", "node-polyfill":"Drop NodePolyfillPlugin from library builds. It injects Buffer, process and console into every extension whether or not anything asked.", "build-tooling":"Build-time code that cannot run in a browser. Keep it out of the module graph.", "already-external":"Shell already externalizes this. Rebuilding against a current shell removes it.", "extension-code":"Not shell's to fix.", "extension-dep":"Not shell's to fix.", "generated":"Generated by the build. Expected.", "webpack-runtime":"Module plumbing. Expected.", "externalized":"Recorded but not bundled. This is the good outcome."}), "causeDescription":"Categories say where a file came from; causes say who put it there, which is the version that maps onto an owner and a change. Everything above the rule is recoverable in rancher/dashboard alone.", "shellCaused":"Shell-caused", "diskNote":"Sizes are source bytes scaled to disk by this bundle's own source-to-disk ratio, so they add up to the shipped size rather than to two or three times it. The ratio is measured per bundle: across the published extensions it runs from 0.30 to 0.66, so one shared figure would be wrong for almost all of them.", "noRatio":"This bundle's source maps carried no content, so source bytes could not be scaled to disk. Sizes below are pre-minification and not comparable with the shipped size.", "tabsCause":"By cause", "cols":({"extension":"Extension", "version":"Version", "chunks":"Chunks", "chunk":"Chunk", "bundleSize":"Bundle size", "size":"Size", "ownCode":"Own code", "externalLibs":"External libs", "shellLeak":"Shell bundled?", "componentsLeak":"Components bundled?", "category":"Category", "cause":"Cause", "fix":"Fix", "package":"Package", "packages":"Packages", "sourceSize":"Source size", "shippedSize":"Shipped size", "shellCaused":"Shell-caused", "ratio":"Ratio", "resolved":"Resolved version", "files":"Files"})}), "bumpImpact":({"title":"Dependency Impact", "description":"Which official extensions a rancher/dashboard dependency bump can reach, joined from the inventory, import and bundle analyses already saved. This page fetches nothing on its own.", "checkHint":"Re-resolves the latest released version of every official extension so out-of-date readings can be spotted. A few seconds, no re-analysis.", "empty":"Paste a Dependabot pull request above, or type a package and the version it is moving to, to see which extensions it reaches.", "noRows":"No extensions found in the saved analyses.", "docs":({"inventory":"lockfile inventory", "imports":"import analysis", "bundles":"bundle analysis"}), "missingDocs":"Never built: {docs}. Extensions missing from an analysis cannot be answered for and will show as unknown. Build the missing ones on their own pages first.", "input":({"prLabel":"Dependabot pull request", "prPlaceholder":"https://github.com/rancher/dashboard/pull/18965, #18965 or 18965", "prSubmit":"Read PR", "prReading":"Reading…", "bumpLabel":"Or add a package by hand", "bumpPlaceholder":"axios@1.8.2", "bumpSubmit":"Add", "clear":"Clear"}), "errors":({"badPr":"That does not look like a pull request. Paste a GitHub PR URL, a #number, or just the number.", "noBumps":"PR #{number} has no Dependabot dependency trailers in any of its commits, so there is nothing to assess. If you know what moved, add the package by hand.", "badBump":"Type a package and the version it is moving to, like axios@1.8.2. The version is required — without one there is nothing to compare against.", "noTarget":"{name} is no longer in the manifest or in any known repository, so there is nothing to re-read it at."}), "summary":({"packages":"Packages bumped", "runtime":"Reached at runtime", "rebuild":"Reached on rebuild", "unknown":"Cannot say", "stale":"Extensions out of date"}), "notChecked":"Nobody has checked whether these readings are still current. Every version below was read at some point in the past and may describe a release that has since been superseded. Press Refresh to resolve each extension's latest release and find out.", "staleFound":"{count} extension(s) have released since they were analysed, so what is saved describes code nobody is running: {extensions}. Their rows read unknown rather than guessing. Re-analyse them from the table below.", "allCurrent":"Every extension was analysed at the version it currently publishes, so the answers below are about code that is actually deployed.", "hostProvided":"Host-provided", "hostProvidedNote":"rancher/dashboard supplies this package to every extension at runtime, so the bump lands on extension versions that are already installed in clusters. The extension's own pin is never used.", "selfResolved":"Extension-resolved", "selfResolvedNote":"Each extension carries its own copy of this package, so the bump reaches an extension only when it next builds against a new shell. Nothing already installed changes.", "prLink":"PR #{number}", "counts":"{runtime} at runtime · {rebuild} on rebuild · {unknown} unknown", "nowAt":"now at {version}", "staleTooltip":"This extension has released since it was analysed, so the saved reading describes code nobody is running. That is why this row says unknown rather than not affected. Re-analyse it to get a real answer.", "unchecked":"not checked", "uncheckedTooltip":"Nobody has confirmed this is still the version the extension publishes. Press Refresh at the top of the page to find out.", "reach":({"runtime":"Runtime", "rebuild":"On rebuild", "none":"Not affected", "unknown":"Unknown"}), "reachNote":({"runtime":"This extension runs the host's copy of the package, so the bump reaches the versions installed in clusters today.", "rebuild":"This extension uses the package but resolves its own copy, so nothing changes for it until it is rebuilt and released.", "none":"Nothing in this extension's lockfile, source or published bundle mentions the package — as it was read at the version in the last column. If that version is out of date this row would say unknown instead, so check that it is current before relying on this.", "unknown":"No answer can be given. Either an analysis is missing this extension, or it was read at a version the extension no longer publishes — in which case the reading describes code nobody is running and cannot support \"not affected\" any more than it supports \"affected\". Expand the row for which it is."}), "skew":({"aligned":"Same minor", "behind-major":"Major behind", "behind-minor":"Minor behind", "ahead":"Ahead", "mixed":"Mixed", "unknown":"—"}), "evidence":({"imports":"imported", "bundled":"in bundle", "lockfileOnly":"lockfile only"}), "gap":({"stale":"Out of date", "not-analysed":"Not in the inventory", "no-lockfile":"Lockfile unreadable", "no-bundle-detail":"No bundle breakdown"}), "gapNote":({"stale":"At least one analysis read this extension at a version it no longer publishes, so its answer describes code nobody is running. Re-analyse it to get a real answer.", "not-analysed":"The lockfile inventory has no row for this extension, so there is nothing to check the package against.", "no-lockfile":"The inventory tried and failed to read this extension's lockfile, so the versions it resolves are unknown.", "no-bundle-detail":"The published bundle was measured but its per-package breakdown was not saved, so the bundle column is blank rather than negative."}), "detail":({"readAt":"Read from {repo} at {versions}.", "fromBranch":"This extension has no released tag, so it was read from a branch head. That reading goes out of date on the next push and nothing here can detect it.", "noGaps":"Every analysis has a current reading for this extension."}), "reanalyse":({"title":"Re-analysing extension", "action":"Re-analyse", "waiting":"Re-analysing…"}), "cols":({"extension":"Extension", "reach":"Reach", "pinned":"Pinned versions", "skew":"Skew", "evidence":"Evidence", "analysed":"Analysed at", "actions":""}), "risk":({"breaking":"Breaking", "watch":"Watch", "safe":"Safe", "unclear":"Unclear"}), "advise":({"action":"$$ Assess with AI", "waiting":"Assessing…", "done":"Assessed", "failed":"Failed", "hint":"Reads each package's GitHub release notes between the versions involved and asks the Claude provider configured in Settings whether the change actually breaks a consumer. Nothing stale or unanalysed is sent — only the package name, the versions, and the extensions with a confirmed path. On the default model, claude-sonnet-4-6, that is roughly 1,500 input and 150 output tokens per package, about half a US cent each.", "pending":"Next press: {count} package(s).", "check":"Check: {check}", "noNotes":"No release notes could be found for this package, so this verdict is based on the version numbers alone.", "noCredentials":"No Claude provider is configured. Add one on the Settings page to use this.", "noBumps":"Add a pull request or a package first — there is nothing to assess yet.", "nothingReached":"Nothing to assess. No package here has a confirmed path to any extension, and asking about one would produce an opinion on an empty question.", "skipped":"Not sent, because nothing verified is affected by them: {packages}."}), "caveats":({"title":"What this can and cannot tell you", "staleness":({"title":"Readings age silently.", "body":"The three analyses are snapshots. An extension that has released since one was built is reported as unknown rather than unaffected, because the saved reading describes code nobody is running — but that only happens once you press Refresh. Before then no claim is made about how current anything is."}), "lockfile":({"title":"Absence is weaker evidence than presence.", "body":"A package found in a lockfile is definitely there. A package not found may still arrive through a dependency whose own lockfile entry was unreadable, or through an extension the inventory has no row for at all."}), "specifiers":({"title":"Imports are recorded by package, not by symbol.", "body":"The import analysis knows that an extension imports a package; it does not record which exports it uses. So nothing here can tell you whether the specific function a release removed was one the extension called."}), "transitive":({"title":"Only direct dependency names are matched.", "body":"A bump is matched against package names as they appear in lockfiles, sources and bundles. A package that reaches an extension only as a transitive dependency of something else is in the lockfile and will match, but nothing here shows you the chain that put it there."}), "branch":({"title":"Some extensions are read from a branch.", "body":"An extension with no released tag is analysed from its default branch head. That reading is correct the moment it is taken and wrong after the next push, and no version check can detect it — the rows say so individually."}), "hostList":({"title":"Host-provided is a fixed list.", "body":"Runtime reach is decided by the same list the bundle analyser uses: shell's own packages plus the five it externalises. If rancher/dashboard changes what it externalises, this page is wrong until that list is updated."}), "model":({"title":"The AI verdict is commentary, never evidence.", "body":"When used, the model is only asked whether a release breaks consumers. It never decides which extensions are affected, never reorders the table and never removes a row — and it is given no stale or unverified row to reason about."})})}), "links":({"title":"Important Links", "description":"Extensions documentation in Confluence."}), "actions":({"title":"Actions", "refreshAll":"Refresh all data", "openSettings":"Open Settings", "openDocs":"Extensions dev docs"}), "settings":({"title":"Settings", "description":"Credentials are stored in the {secret} Secret in the {namespace} namespace. They are never displayed again once saved.", "githubToken":({"label":"GitHub Personal Access Token", "placeholder":"ghp_…", "tooltip":"Needs public_repo (or repo for private repos) plus read:org. Used for all GitHub API calls so the dashboard is not rate limited."}), "provider":({"sectionTitle":"Claude Provider", "sectionHint":"Optional. Used by the Describe with AI action on the Known Extension Repos page, which writes a short description and a category for every community repo. Without it that page falls back to repo metadata.", "label":"Provider", "tooltip":"Credentials are kept per provider, so switching back and forth does not make you re-enter them.", "options":({"anthropic":"Anthropic API", "vertex":"Claude on Google Vertex AI", "claudeAws":"Claude Platform on AWS"})}), "anthropicKey":({"label":"Anthropic API Key", "placeholder":"sk-ant-…", "tooltip":"Create one at console.anthropic.com. The key is sent straight from your browser to the Anthropic API."}), "vertex":({"serviceAccount":({"label":"Credentials JSON", "placeholder":"'{' \"type\": \"service_account\", … '}'", "tooltip":"Either a service account key downloaded from the Google Cloud console, or the file \"gcloud auth application-default login\" writes. Paste it verbatim. Whichever you use needs the Vertex AI User role, and is exchanged for a token in your browser — the key itself is never sent anywhere. Prefer a service account: the gcloud file is your personal Google identity, and it is stored in a Secret that other cluster admins can read."}), "examples":({"intro":"Paste one whole file, exactly as you got it. Either of these works — the JSON below shows the fields that are read, with the rest left out.", "serviceAccount":"A service account key. Google Cloud console › IAM & Admin › Service Accounts › pick the account › Keys › Add key › Create new key › JSON.", "authorizedUser":"Your own credentials. Run \"gcloud auth application-default login\", then paste ~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json.", "note":"Both are stored in a Secret that other cluster administrators can read, so a service account scoped to Vertex AI User is the safer of the two — the gcloud file is your personal Google identity."}), "projectId":({"label":"GCP Project ID", "tooltip":"The project the model is enabled in and the calls are billed to. This is the project ID, not the project number or the display name."}), "region":({"label":"Location", "tooltip":"\"global\", a multi-region (\"us\", \"eu\") or a region (\"us-east5\"). The model has to be enabled for this project in Model Garden for the location you pick, or the call comes back as a 404 that reads like the model does not exist."}), "proxyNote":"Google refuses browser calls to Vertex, so this one provider is routed through Rancher's proxy. That needs a cluster-scoped ProxyEndpoint, which is created for you if you are an administrator — otherwise ask one to add the Vertex host for your location."}), "claudeAws":({"apiKey":({"label":"Workspace API Key", "tooltip":"Create one in the AWS console under Claude Platform on AWS, then API keys. An Amazon Bedrock key will not work here — the two are separate services with separate endpoints and separate keys."}), "workspaceId":({"label":"Workspace ID", "placeholder":"wrkspc_…", "tooltip":"Required on every call and not derivable from the key. Find it under Workspaces on the Claude Platform on AWS console page."}), "region":({"label":"AWS Region", "tooltip":"Part of the endpoint hostname, so it has to be a region your account is set up in. A region you have no endpoint in still resolves in DNS, so getting it wrong fails as a connection error rather than an API one. There is no default."})}), "model":({"label":"Model Override", "tooltip":"Leave blank to use the default shown. All three providers take the same first-party model IDs; Vertex spells a dated snapshot with an @ instead of a hyphen, which is handled for you.", "hint":"Blank uses {model}, which is a good fit for writing one-line repo descriptions. For the strongest model, write {strongest}."}), "test":({"label":"Test connection", "waiting":"Calling…", "success":"Reached", "error":"Failed", "ok":"Connection works. The model replied: {reply}", "failed":"Connection failed: {message}", "needsCredentials":"Fill in the credentials for the selected provider to test them.", "hint":"Calls {model} rather than the model above, to keep the check cheap. On Vertex that model has to be enabled in Model Garden too, so a failure here with everything else working may just mean it is not."}), "configured":"Configured", "notConfigured":"Not configured", "save":"Save", "saving":"Saving…", "saved":"Credentials saved.", "clear":"Clear", "cleared":"Credentials cleared.", "saveFailed":"Could not save credentials: {message}", "permissionDenied":"You do not have permission to manage Secrets in the {namespace} namespace. Ask a cluster administrator to configure this extension.", "leaveBlank":"Leave blank to keep the current value."}), "security":({"title":"Security", "description":"Known vulnerabilities in the extension catalogue repos, the two published NPM packages and every official extension, and how those counts have moved over time.", "allRepos":"All repos", "loading":"Reading vulnerabilities…", "empty":"No known vulnerabilities for the current filters.", "noPatch":"No patch", "manifestFailed":"Could not read the official extensions manifest, so only the catalogue repos are listed: {message}", "noHistory":"No history for this repo. The chart is reconstructed from the dates Dependabot records against each alert, and public dependency data carries no such dates — it describes the tree as it stands today and nothing more.", "cache":({"stale":"This data is over a day old — see the timestamp above. Press Refresh to re-read it.", "overdue":"This data is more than {days} days old. Vulnerability counts change daily, so re-read it before acting on anything below.", "writeFailed":"Could not save this data, so the next visit will read it from scratch: {message}"}), "severity":({"critical":"Critical", "high":"High", "medium":"Medium", "low":"Low", "unknown":"Unknown"}), "scope":({"runtime":"Runtime", "development":"Development", "mixed":"Mixed"}), "relationship":({"direct":"Direct", "transitive":"Transitive"}), "source":({"dependabot":"Dependabot", "public":"Public data"}), "view":({"list":"List", "chart":"Over time"}), "range":({"90":"3 months", "182":"6 months", "365":"1 year", "label":"Range", "all":"All"}), "age":({"days":"{count} days", "months":"{count} months", "years":"{count} years"}), "summary":({"severityTitle":"Open advisories", "remediationTitle":"Remediation"}), "tiles":({"oldest":"Oldest open"}), "filters":({"all":"All", "severity":"Severity", "scope":"Scope", "triage":"Next step", "exposure":"Exposure"}), "triage":({"fix-ready":({"label":"Needs a PR", "short":"Need a PR", "description":"A fixed version is published and no open pull request moves to it, so nothing is in flight. This is the work."}), "in-review":({"label":"PR open", "short":"In review", "description":"An open Dependabot pull request already bumps this package to the fixed version or past it. It needs a reviewer, not a fix."}), "no-fix":({"label":"No fix yet", "short":"No fix yet", "description":"The advisory has no published fixed version, so there is nothing to upgrade to. Track it; it cannot be closed from here."})}), "exposure":({"shipped":({"label":"Shipped"}), "tooling":({"label":"Tooling"}), "unknown":({"label":"Unknown"}), "note":"Build tooling — the alert is against {segment}/, which users never download."}), "prError":"Could not read this repository's open pull requests, so no finding can be shown as already in review and some below will overstate the work left: {error}", "cols":({"package":"Package", "triage":"Next step", "severity":"Severity", "advisories":"Advisories", "manifests":"Manifests", "patched":"Patched in", "scope":"Scope", "oldest":"Oldest", "repo":"Repository", "source":"Source", "vulnerabilities":"Vulnerabilities", "total":"Total", "reach":"Ships?", "inBundles":"In bundles", "shippedBytes":"Shipped size", "flaggedBy":"Flagged by"}), "manifestCount":"{count} manifests", "reach":({"tab":"By package", "explain":"Every other tab is organised by repository, which is how the advisories arrive and not how the risk is spread. This one crosses the vulnerable packages against what the published bundles on gh-pages actually contain, so a package appears once and is ranked by whether it reaches a browser. Most of what a lockfile flags never ships — build tooling, test harnesses, dependencies that tree-shaking removed — and those are hygiene, not exposure.", "empty":"Nothing vulnerable was found in any published bundle.", "noBundles":"Bundle analysis has never been run, so there is nothing to cross these advisories against. Run it from the Bundle Analysis page first.", "noRepos":"No repositories have been read yet. Open a repo tab, or load the whole estate from the All repos tab, and the packages will appear here.", "scope":"Across {repos} repos and {bundles} analysed bundles", "notShippedNote":"This package is in no published bundle. Still worth fixing, but it is not something a user downloads.", "resolved":"Resolved: {value}", "noLockfile":"No lockfile read", "stats":({"confirmed":"ship a vulnerable version", "unconfirmed":"ship, version unconfirmed", "notShipped":"do not ship"}), "verdict":({"hit":"Ships", "partial":"Ships (one of several)", "unknown":"Ships, unconfirmed", "miss":"Not shipped"})}), "shellUpgrade":({"tab":"Shell upgrade", "explain":"Extensions do not load @rancher/shell from Rancher at runtime — it is compiled into each published bundle, so every release freezes a copy of shell and of the versions shell pinned that day. That makes upgrading shell a real fix, and this puts a number on it: what each extension actually shipped, and how many of its open findings a bump would clear.", "floor":"Counts are a floor, not a total. Shell declares its direct dependencies only, so anything a bump clears deeper in the tree is not visible here.", "target":"Measured against @rancher/shell {version}", "includePrereleases":"Include pre-releases", "load":"Read shipped shell versions", "loading":"Reading releases…", "empty":"No official extensions to measure.", "noRepos":"No repositories have been read yet, so there are no findings to credit a bump with. The versions and dropped dependencies below are still accurate; open a repo tab or load the whole estate to fill in the rest.", "cols":({"extension":"Extension", "shipped":"Shell shipped", "cleared":"Findings cleared", "removed":"Dependencies dropped"}), "current":"up to date", "currentNote":"This release already ships {version}, so there is nothing to gain.", "atLeast":"at least {count}", "unknownShort":"Could not read", "unknown":({"no-lockfile":"This release has no yarn.lock in it, so there is no record of which shell version was compiled into the bundle.", "not-in-lockfile":"A yarn.lock was read but it does not resolve @rancher/shell, so the shipped version cannot be established from it.", "unreadable":"The release's file listing could not be read. Its GitHub release name and its git tag sometimes differ, in which case nothing resolves at the ref the manifest points at."}), "source":"Read from {lockfile}: {from} → {to}", "noneCleared":"No open finding in this repository is against a package shell pins, so the bump clears nothing that is currently reported.", "how":({"removed":"dropped by shell at {target}", "repinned":"shell pins {version}"}), "removedTitle":"{count} dependencies shell no longer declares:"}), "search":({"tab":"Find a package", "explain":"Every other tab starts from a published advisory. This one starts from a name, which is how an incident actually arrives — usually hours before anything is filed against it. It searches the complete resolved lockfile of every official extension, not just what reaches a bundle, because most supply-chain attacks run from a postinstall script and never touch a browser.", "label":"Package", "placeholder":"lodash, or lodash@<4.17.21", "submit":"Search", "cols":({"extension":"Extension", "resolved":"Resolved version", "inRange":"In range?", "ships":"Ships?", "release":"Release"}), "range":"against {range}", "scope":"Found in {found} of {searched} extensions", "notFound":"{name} is not in any of the {searched} extension lockfiles that were searched.", "notFoundShort":"No extension resolves this package.", "didYouMean":"Close matches:", "unreadable":"No lockfile could be read for {extensions}, so this answer does not cover them. Refresh the inventory, and if it keeps failing treat those extensions as unknown rather than as clear.", "ships":"Ships", "buildOnly":"Build only", "noBundles":"Bundle analysis has never been run, so whether this package reaches a published bundle is unknown. Run it from the Bundle Analysis page.", "cause":"Pulled into the bundle by {cause}.", "readFrom":"Read from {repo} at {ref}, {lockfile}", "head":"HEAD", "fromBranch":"No lockfile resolved at the release ref, so this was read from {ref} — the current branch, not what was shipped.", "verdict":({"hit":"In range", "partial":"One of several", "unknown":"Unconfirmed", "miss":"Out of range"}), "stale":"The package inventory was built over a day ago, so a dependency bumped since then is not reflected. Refresh before acting on an empty result.", "needsBuild":"The package inventory has not been built yet. It reads one lockfile per extension — a few seconds, and none of it against the GitHub rate limit — and is then stored for the next visit.", "build":"Build package inventory", "building":"Reading lockfiles…", "coverage":"Searching {count} extension lockfiles, {packages} distinct packages"}), "detail":({"range":"Vulnerable: {value}", "patched":"Fixed in: {value}", "vulnerable":"Vulnerable", "manifest":"Manifest", "relationship":"Dependency", "scope":"Scope", "reported":"Reported", "fixedIn":"Fixed in {value}", "noFix":"No patch available", "ghsaLink":"View {value} on GitHub", "cveLink":"View {value} in the National Vulnerability Database", "pr":"Open PR #{number}", "prLink":"#{number} {title}", "prDraft":"draft", "remediation":"Fix", "remediationIn":"Add to {file}", "copy":"Copy the fix"}), "publicSource":({"title":"Source: public data, not Dependabot", "detail":"The configured GitHub token cannot read the Dependabot alerts for this repo, so these rows come from its public dependency graph matched against the OSV advisory database. That means no dismissals are honoured, nothing is deduplicated the way Dependabot does it, and there is no runtime versus development split — so these counts run higher and are not comparable with the counts on a Dependabot repo. Advisories that carry no severity rating at all are counted as Unknown rather than being graded down to Low.", "unresolved":"{count} dependencies were declared as a version range the dependency graph never resolved. They are excluded rather than guessed at."}), "rollup":({"explain":"The estate view reads all {count} repos, which takes around a minute and a few hundred requests. Individual tabs are much cheaper, so this one is on request rather than automatic.", "load":"Load all security data", "loading":"Loading…", "dependabot":"From Dependabot", "publicData":"From public data", "repoCount":"{count} repos", "failed":"Could not read: {repos}"}), "scopeNote":({"shell":"This package lives in rancher/dashboard rather than a repo of its own. Dependabot records the lockfile each alert was raised against, and shell has one, so these rows are the alerts filed against shell/yarn.lock and nothing else in the monorepo.", "components":"This package lives in rancher/dashboard and no longer has a lockfile of its own, so its transitive dependencies resolve through the workspace root and Dependabot files them against the root yarn.lock along with the whole monorepo. These rows are everything filed against pkg/rancher-components, plus the root lockfile alerts for packages that its package.json declares under dependencies or peerDependencies. That covers its direct dependencies; anything transitive pulled in since the lockfile was removed cannot be told apart from the rest of the monorepo, so treat this as a floor rather than a complete picture."})})})})];
